# ENT-12 — Backup & Disaster Recovery Automation

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/backup-disaster-recovery-automation-governance.md`.
Governance section `backup_dr_governance`; readiness `foundation:backup-dr-check --strict`.

- Automated DB backup runs through `scripts/backup-vps.sh`: fail-fast `pg_dump`
  → `foundation:backup-verify` → prune by `BACKUP_DR_RETENTION_DAYS` (keep a
  minimum floor). No destructive DB command.
- Restore rehearsal runs through `scripts/restore-rehearsal.sh` into a scratch
  database that MUST differ from the production database; it aborts otherwise,
  drops only the scratch DB, and never restores over the pilot.
- Production data restore is the separate, explicit
  `scripts/restore_postgres.sh` step — never automatic.
- RTO/RPO objectives and retention are documented in `config/backup_dr.php`.
- `backup-dr-check.json` is required in the ci/vps release-evidence profiles and
  `foundation:backup-dr-check` is a pre-deploy gate; evidence stays non-sensitive
  (path/size/counts only, no secret/PII/KTP/NIK).
- Any new backup/DR automation must extend the ENT-12 contract with tests and
  pass `foundation:backup-dr-check` before shipping.
- Never `migrate:fresh` / `db:wipe` on the VPS; `migrate --force` only.
